WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.800
- It's time for another
segment of "Designed by Drew",

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.810
where we get to create

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.155
a brand new space for incredible people.

00:00:08.155 --> 00:00:10.470
And today's Designed by Drew viewer,

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.240
I think she's here for some design advice,

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.370
and has no idea that we
actually have a brand new room

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.498
waiting for her behind those doors.

00:00:19.498 --> 00:00:21.150
(sharp giggles)

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:24.270
Okay, first, let's meet the mom

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.180
whose strength and positivity

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.721
are truly inspiring, take a look.

00:00:29.721 --> 00:00:32.888
(gentle upbeat music)

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.200
- My name's Kerin Mackechnie,
I live in Scarborough, Maine,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.550
I have two little boys, Jack and Drew,

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:41.780
who are six and nine years old.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.283
I met Ian, we were both 22 years old,

00:00:44.283 --> 00:00:48.620
and within about an hour or
so, I knew he was the one,

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.067
and I leaned over and
whispered in my friend's ear,

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:52.767
"This is the guy I'm gonna marry."

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:59.360
The happiest that Ian and I
have ever been was that summer

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.850
when we first moved into
our house in Scarborough,

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.090
it's our dream home,

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.930
and we put in a lot of love

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:07.370
into pretty much every single room

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.600
except for our master bedroom.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.667
Our thought was, "That's the only room

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:12.807
"that nobody goes in, but us,

00:01:12.807 --> 00:01:15.167
"so, let's put all our
time and effort and money

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.807
"into the rest of the house."

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:21.630
We knew we needed to buy
some new decorative items

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.780
and kind of spruce the
pace up, make it our own,

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.620
and so, I went to Christmas tree shop

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.210
on the tight budget I was on.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.987
And so, I came home with this
sailboat painting and I said,

00:01:29.987 --> 00:01:33.777
"Ian, someday, my bedroom
will match this painting,

00:01:33.777 --> 00:01:36.140
"and this will work on the
walls in there and it will go,"

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:39.087
and he was like, "Okay, all
right, someday, not now,

00:01:39.087 --> 00:01:40.205
"but I agree, someday."

00:01:40.205 --> 00:01:42.030
One of the happiest days of our lives

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:43.740
was the day that Drew was born,

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.650
but it was the day after
that in the hospital

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.047
that Ian's mom looked at him and said,

00:01:48.047 --> 00:01:52.367
"Your coloring looks
off, it looks different,

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:54.510
"and I think you should
go get it checked out,"

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:57.440
and he was diagnosed with leiomyosarcoma.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.696
His reaction was always,
"Okay, so what do I do next?"

00:02:01.696 --> 00:02:04.520
No chemo scared him, no surgery,

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.090
he just wanted to know what was next,

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.775
he wanted to beat it,
and he wanted to beat it

00:02:08.775 --> 00:02:11.160
because he had two little boys at home

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:16.090
and he had me, and he had
this whole life ahead of us.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.090
I remember saying goodbye to Ian

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.880
when I had to bring him
to the hospice house,

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.233
and I knew he was never gonna
come back to this house,

00:02:23.233 --> 00:02:25.363
and I remember saying to him,

00:02:26.847 --> 00:02:28.426
"We painted every wall,

00:02:28.426 --> 00:02:31.183
"we've done everything
to this house together,

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:34.196
"you will always be in
this house with us."

00:02:34.196 --> 00:02:35.520
(soft ambient music)

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:39.260
Ian is a part of our
life every single day,

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.014
everything's daddy this, daddy that,

00:02:41.014 --> 00:02:43.710
we have photo montage videos of him

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.417
that my kids will say, "Friday
night, instead of a movie,

00:02:46.417 --> 00:02:48.079
"can we watch daddy's video?"

00:02:48.079 --> 00:02:50.109
And we have a lot of fun,

00:02:50.109 --> 00:02:52.330
there's no way I can waste this life

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.095
that Jack and Drew and I have together

00:02:54.095 --> 00:02:57.170
on not being happy and enjoying
everything we get to see

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:58.561
and everything we get to experience,

00:02:58.561 --> 00:03:01.923
it's hard, but they can't
not do that for him.

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:07.377
(crowd applauding)

00:03:08.956 --> 00:03:10.345
- Okay.

00:03:10.345 --> 00:03:11.800
(Kerin giggles)

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.577
Why, and how do you know

00:03:14.577 --> 00:03:18.500
that positivity really
has an answer for you

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.712
or could be an answer for anyone?

00:03:20.712 --> 00:03:23.253
- I don't think there's
really any other option.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:28.165
Life's short, things happen
that you have no idea,

00:03:28.165 --> 00:03:30.315
you don't know what
tomorrow's gonna bring,

00:03:31.371 --> 00:03:34.841
so, I live every day knowing that

00:03:34.841 --> 00:03:36.730
a lot of bad can happen,

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:38.950
whether it's cancer, whether it's COVID,

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:40.670
life can change on a whirlwind,

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.390
and staying positive

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:46.172
and trying to be the best
person you can be and be happy,

00:03:46.172 --> 00:03:49.383
why not? Why would you not wanna do that?

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.223
- I couldn't agree more.

00:03:54.538 --> 00:03:57.840
When a choice doesn't seem easy that day,

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.630
what do you turn to,

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:03.600
to go and get back to that positivity?

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.130
- Yeah, for me, honestly,

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:08.010
it's that Ian doesn't even
have that choice anymore,

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.683
and I have these two little boys

00:04:09.683 --> 00:04:12.250
who were four and six when
their dad passed away,

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:14.690
and their dad is, and always will be,

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.140
and should be their hero.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:22.140
And I live every day and
there's things I get to see,

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.750
and experience, and do,
and laugh, and have fun,

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:29.740
and Ian would give anything
to do those things with us

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.705
and watching someone go through cancer

00:04:31.705 --> 00:04:34.852
to watch someone who is
saying, "Okay, what's next?

00:04:34.852 --> 00:04:36.357
"Okay, I'll do that chemo.

00:04:36.357 --> 00:04:38.360
"Sure. I'll try that surgery."

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:41.307
How can I not now live and be like,

00:04:41.307 --> 00:04:42.572
"Of course, I'm gonna have fun,"

00:04:42.572 --> 00:04:44.560
he made these horrible choices

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.240
just because he wanted
to be able to have fun

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:47.941
and continue to have fun someday.

00:04:47.941 --> 00:04:52.941
I'm healthy, I'm able to have
that fun with Jack and Drew,

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:58.120
and show them that life
can be really hard,

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:02.410
and it's just about looking
at what you can change,

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:03.895
what you can be in control of,

00:05:03.895 --> 00:05:08.895
and finding the positives,
being happy and being kind.

00:05:09.027 --> 00:05:12.510
- I know in honoring your home,

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:15.911
you've taken care of the kids' spaces,

00:05:15.911 --> 00:05:20.790
and you've fixed up everything
and done your little things,

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:25.790
and you've left this bedroom
sort of as a last step,

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:30.000
and I would imagine that
changing the bedroom

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.377
probably has a lot of emotional
ties to it as well now,

00:05:34.377 --> 00:05:37.757
is there any conflict
or does it seem like,

00:05:37.757 --> 00:05:39.050
"Okay, it's time?"

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.910
What is going on in you?

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:42.380
What's your inner dialogue?

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:45.390
- So, 2020 was like kind
of a turning point for me,

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:46.440
going into 2020,

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.790
and at the beginning of the year,

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:50.690
his clothes were still everywhere,

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:53.530
my closet was half my
clothes, half his clothes.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:56.400
And I finally, I think
it was after COVID hit

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.550
where it was like we're
all now in our homes

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:00.540
and kind of analyzing and
thinking about our lives

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.150
even in a deeper level,

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:03.517
and it was sort of like,

00:06:03.517 --> 00:06:07.570
"I think I'm ready to put these away,"

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.700
they're in the basement in bins,

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:10.876
they're not going anywhere,

00:06:10.876 --> 00:06:12.810
but they're not in my bedroom,

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:14.750
so, that was my first big step.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.767
And then next has been,

00:06:16.767 --> 00:06:19.549
"Okay, I gotta get rid of the stripes."

00:06:19.549 --> 00:06:21.280
(both chuckle softly)

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.040
My yeah...

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.670
I've now at the point where I think Ian...

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.910
I know that Ian wants me to be happy,

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.570
and I think that any positive thing

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:31.760
that happens to me and the kids,

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:36.563
I do believe that he can
see me, I think he sees us.

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:41.030
I choose to believe that,
I have to believe that,

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:42.960
that he sees all the things
that Jack and Drew do,

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.250
and that I do,

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.880
and I think he'd be really happy and ready

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:50.497
that I'm now mentally in
a place where I can say,

00:06:50.497 --> 00:06:55.220
"Okay, I can make this what
we always wanted it to be."

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:58.310
It goes along with the whole 2020 for me,

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:00.030
moving forward and making these strides

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:01.744
that I really wasn't able to do.

00:07:01.744 --> 00:07:05.140
He passed away in 2018,
I wasn't able to do that

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:08.500
until I all of a sudden
was, and that's okay.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:11.250
- I think it's just incredibly
healthy and I'd be honored

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:14.320
to discuss it with you, I live for design.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.318
- I've heard that and I
think that sounds amazing.

00:07:16.318 --> 00:07:17.290
(Kerin laughs)

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.110
I'll take any advice I can get.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.040
- Perfect. And I know
where your heart is at,

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.150
so, we're gonna do this
respectfully and thoughtfully.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:24.060
- Perfect.

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:27.227
(gentle upbeat music)

